1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,893
Every answer AI gives you runs on electricity.

2
00:00:03,943 --> 00:00:06,386
Data centres used to just store things.

3
00:00:06,436 --> 00:00:08,866
Photos. Videos. Web pages.

4
00:00:08,916 --> 00:00:12,441
But now they think — and thinking takes power.

5
00:00:12,491 --> 00:00:16,334
Last year, data centres used 485 terawatt-hours.

6
00:00:16,384 --> 00:00:21,572
By 2030: almost double — about 3% of the world’s electricity.

7
00:00:21,622 --> 00:00:23,328
And the AI part triples.

8
00:00:23,378 --> 00:00:27,593
So the next limit on AI may not be chips… but power.

9
00:00:27,643 --> 00:00:30,493
Who gets the power — and who pays the bill?
